==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Ururun Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Awakened Ururun''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP after completing [[Eldritch Forces]].

==Strategy/Usage==
Ururun Wolf is a decent backliner. While having Knockback, she is more used as a DPS dealer more than crowd-control because of the knockback's low activation chance. Her range is also almost the same as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]], so she is sufficient to deal with [[Le'boin]] and most of his variants. Sometimes her knockback may backfire, such as in backliner-heavy stages and against [[Idi:Re]].

She does rapid attacks, which is very consistent for a backliner. She also has enough damage to force [[Gory Dark]], [[Rain D.]] and [[Shadow Boxer K]] to flinch, effectively stun-locking them.

However, Ururun Wolf has low health, long recharge and high cost, which makes her frustrating to use sometimes, as enemies may exploit her mediocre survivability to kill her long before a replacement could be sent. Comparing her to other backliners, her 4.2k DPS is rather below average, but since she is a free unit, she is quite helpful for early-game, and also attacks much faster than many backliner Ubers, although that still doesn't excuse the fact that some units like [[Thunder God Zeus (Uber Rare Cat)|The Majestic Zeus]] do better than her. Overall, Ururun Wolf is just a simple DPS backliner used as another ranged unit.

==='''True Form'''===
Awakened Ururun increases her DPS enough to reach the average Uber Rare. However, her health remains subpar. Combined with her long recharge time, she remains fragile and awkward to use. Her abilities and extra range are rather convenient, however.

More of a yardstick than an actual unit, Awakened Ururun largely functions as something to measure other backline Ubers against, with failure to reach it being an issue even for specialists. Common in guides for accessibility purposes, most of the time she should be replaced with a backline Uber you happen to have. 4-Crown SoL is where she'll shine most due to minimal competition, though even then not that much.

Beyond SoL, however, her use will drop significantly, since her health becomes a greater weakness and you will eventually get access to [[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Awakened Urs]] near the end of UL, which can replace Ururun entirely. But she still has some viable use in non-SoL stages where backliners with high DPS are needed, such as [[Adherence to Virtue]], and she can be used in tandem with Urs for best results of DPS too. Make sure to level her up to max so she can survive some decently strong hits, though.

{{Job|Classification = Backliner}}

