==Trivia==
*Ururun is the name of the rider, not the mount.
**The unit originally consisted of only the wolf, but art director Tamasan later added Ururun due to feeling that the wolf was [https://x.com/tamasanp/status/1839870225363415426 lonely].
*Ururun's clothing was very likely based on the female Kirin Armor from the ''[[wikipedia:Monster Hunter|Monster Hunter]]'' series.
**She could also be a reference to [[wikia:ghibli:San|San]] from the Studio Ghibli film ''[[wikipedia:Princess Mononoke|Princess Mononoke]]'', especially with her [[True Form]]'s red mask.
*Ururun Wolf gained the [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] target in [[Version 2.9.1 Update|Version 2.9.1]]. Typically this happens in the same update as the trait is introduced, but Angel was added in [[Version 2.7 Update|Version 2.7]].
*Based on [[The Ururuvu Journals]]' Japanese name, Ururun was most likely named after the Japanese travel show ''[[wikipedia:ja:世界ウルルン滞在記|Sekai Ururun Taizaiki]]'' (世界ウルルン滞在記, "World Ururun Travelogue"), in which a TV personality has to stay with a local family abroad for a week.
*The Japanese name of her Evolved Form's mount, Tama, is simply a common name for pet cats in Japan. It could also be a reference to [[PONOS Corporation|PONOS]] art director Tamasan.
*Ururun is implied to be the daughter of [[Masked Yulala (Special Cat)|Masked Yulala]], given the similar hair, masks, electric-based attacks, and the mention that her father is a teacher at a school, while Yulala is mentioned to have a 12-year old daughter. In [[Sacrifice Apprenticeship]], they even appear together.
**This would also make Ururun the granddaughter of [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Master Uril]], as [[Mystic Mask Yulala]]'s Japanese description calls him the head of his clan while [[Master Uril (Enemy)|enemy Master Uril]]'s Japanese description says he passed down that same title to his son when he retired.
*[[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Urs]] is potentially an ancestor of Ururun, as referred to in the ending of [[Stories of Legend]].
*Ururun Wolf's, Masked Yulala's, Master Uril's and Urs & Fenrir's Japanese descriptions all start with a quote followed by how they joined the Cat Army, which always includes the word 勝手 (''katte'', meaning "selfish", "self-serving" or "acting on one's own without asking").
*Among the masked [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cats]] (Ururun Wolf, [[Hermit Cat (Special Cat)|Masked Grandmaster Cat]], Masked Yulala, Master Uril, Urs & Fenrir, [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Elder Mask Doron]] and [[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Ape Lord Luza]]), Ururun is the only one without a [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] enemy counterpart (counting her separately from Urs).
*Ururun and [[Kuu (Uber Rare Cat)|Kuu]] seem to be on poor terms with each other. [[Jungle Women (Combo)|Jungle Women]]'s Japanese name, Ken'en no Naka (犬猿の仲), literally translates to "Dog-monkey Relationship" and refers to a contentious relationship characterized by mutual hatred or extremely poor relations, like the rivalry between dogs and monkeys.
*According to [[Troubled Youth (Combo)|Troubled Youth]]'s Japanese name, Ururun and [[Akira (Uber Rare Cat)|Akira]] are examples of ''[[wikipedia:Chūnibyō|chūnibyō]]'' (中二病), a slang term essentially describing a delusional teenager (most commonly a 2nd-year middle-schooler) or young adult who to tries to stand out through various stereotypical behaviors such as acting like a pretentious know-it-all, making believe they have special powers and/or pretending to be anti-social. This is further supported by Ururun Cat's description, which states that she is delusional.
*The [[Hunting Club (Combo)|Hunting Club]] [[Cat Combo|Combo]] implies that Ururun is the "best friend who travels with a beast" mentioned in [[Terun (Uber Rare Cat)|Terun]]'s Japanese description.
*Awakened Ururun's English description references the tsundere stock phrase, "It's not like I like you or anything, baka!"
**''Baka'' is a Japanese word meaning "stupid" or "idiot".
*Even though her description says "knocks back enemies", she only knocks back non-[[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies.
*Ururun Wolf and [[Tricycle Cat (Special Cat)|Tricycle Cat]] are tied for the highest amount of [[Cat Combo]]s in the game at 8.
*In The Battle Cats POP!, since [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] is a 100% chance reward for the first-time when completing the game, Treasure Radars cannot be used to obtain Ururun Wolf, forcing the player to deal with the 5% chance to unlock her.
**She is also the only Stories of Legend drop unit to appear in The Battle Cats POP!.

